Interview with a South African. And there was an unexpected change in the middle of the interview - 1aviagem.com
Interview with a South African. And there was an unexpected change in the middle of the interview.
The best way to do that would be to do it like this, for a cell phone to record and that's it. Lexiegh is this wonderful person I met on a 7-hour bus ride and a flat tire halfway through South Africa.
- We met on a bus from Joburg (Johannesburg) to Durbain and we are going to do an interview about South Africa. About some particularities we have here.
- Very good. And people come here to South Africa…
- Yes, like me, first for tourism, to explore, see the animals (on a safari) and the like. But I believe South Africa goes beyond that.
So back to the Apartheid issue, there's the same problem here (misinformation). I think we have come a long way, as we have South Africans since Nelson Mandela was released from prison.
- Very well. So I believe it's getting better, right ?
The beach is my favorite place!
- The beach in Durbain!
- There in Brazil, we have something similar ... not exactly that, not so deep the meaning. But those who believe in Yemanja at the turn of the year jump seven waves and throw a flower overboard.
"And you were evidence of that!"
I would like us to see each other as people. That people lived together well.
- Guys, if you're watching this… I met this guy TODAY!
I met him today, but he seemed to me to be a good person, harmonic, and since then we are dealing with it, getting along. I felt his energy and thought… He's someone I could live with.
An example: we tried to get a Uber to get here, but the app didn't work. So they tried to charge more than twice the price, merely because she was with a white man.
"That's when she explained the situation to me, and I didn't want to believe it." But then the app went back to work and the value came up, and it was less than half what they wanted to charge us.
"And Brazilians, if you come to South Africa, buy a data card from here." Because you don't have Wifi anywhere yet.
But look, we're having dinner now! I'm having dinner with someone I met today!
- Oh, you look so beautiful when you smile!
- See, that's why it's bad to be white, because you get red!
- And if we get sick we turn green.
I say, you didn't come here for nothing. You must have wanted to see something.
Well, if you could change one thing all over the world, no matter where you are from or where you are, what would you change?
I believe everyone has to have faith in something. Whether in God or in a person ... because having faith is necessary.
Okay and then I'll answer that last question too and we're done.
… It would be the way we perceive others.
So guys, if you are watching this, please know that there is nothing greater than love, than respect, and nothing better than knowing "Jonh"!
Because this is what Brazilians do!
