E Where is the Eighth Continent?
In the search for satellite images to know the size of the burns in Brazil as a whole. That is, including the main 6 Brazilian biomes such as: Amazon, Cerrado, Pantanal, Caatinga, Atlantic Forest and Pampas.
In addition to the satellites and their fragments through the site it is possible to track meteorites as well and their trajectory. For example, in the next image you need to see the fragments that came loose from the Thorad Delta 1 DEB satellite (launched on defragmenting 1970).
Since our country is on fire?
The problem is that today there are already more than 7,5 thousand tons of satellites and fragments, ie space debris. And the problem is that the fragment of a satellite that is no longer working, or a piece of a North Korean, Russian, or even American rocket, could eventually hit a working satellite and make it stop working.
And what does this have to do with the Amazon?
It would be joining forces between ministries and nations. Maybe we could put out the fires before they incinerate our biodiversity.
I miss when we only had one satellite around the earth.
In a previous post we did an interview with a Peruvian and a Brazilian tourist about Peru. (You can access this great interview by clicking here).
Due to the altitude on account of the Andes Mountains and other mountains; in at least half of the Peruvian territory (which is above 2.500 meters high) coca leaf tea is taken to relieve the malaise such as: nausea, difficulty breathing and headaches.
Hence the importance of coca leaf and its anesthetic properties. Before anyone gets excited about going there and thinks they'll enjoy a "cheap" or "breeze," or general hallucinogenic effects over tea, the answer is ... no, you're not going to get high.
In addition the coca leaf acts as prevention of ulcer and gastritis, also improves the functioning of the liver and vesicles. And it's important to remember that it will not heal you from all of this, it helps you to improve.
Also serves as a stimulant, combat headaches, diuretic, combat dizziness.
Talking About South American Culture So if you go to Peru, Bolivia, Chile or other countries that have an altitude above 3.000 meters take a little coca tea, but the leaf this will help you a lot!
And you also will not be feeling a "breeze," or hallucinations over coffee.
But it's easy to remember that everything else is poison. If you drink too much coffee you will have a heart attack, if you drink too much coca tea, you will have stomach pain.
But if you are vacationing in these countries or going to climb a mountain, or protect yourself from the cold, then try the taste of the local culture, a little cafe warms you up and awakens you. A coca tea also helps you feel good.
In fact, as a last tip for a first-time sailor who is traveling through South America and wants to taste both Colombian coffee and Peruvian tea I leave the Bookaway link in which it is very simple and easy to schedule an online trip. Note, you can change the language by clicking the flag.
