Then on the bus he starts talking about this statue. his name is Roland and he is nothing more than the chief templar knight who defended the kingdom of Riga.
Not only that, some of his ships are said to have been sunk into the Daugava River with much of their wealth at the behest of the French king who owed Roland a large amount of money.
In addition to Roland were other Templar knights who protected Riga. Yes, these other statues lead us to believe that in the thirteenth century it was the other Knights Templar who gathered in this place.
And this was the seal of the city in the thirteenth century. Riga stamp.
It began with the keys, then a fortress in the background until it arrived at the latter (11), which is the same present on the shield of Roland's statue.
But there you can confirm some of these stories.
They gained fame and notoriety. At first they lived on donations from both locals and kings who used their escort services to go to Jerusalem.
There were many thieves and looters along the way, and many kings traveled with their riches in the chariots. The personal guard did not have the same knowledge of the terrain as the knights.
Or the new Portuguese Order that arose from the Templars. Since there was a ban on using the previous name.
And remember that Roland had a French lineage.
A great example is the symbol on blackheads. House of the black heads.
And already predicting that they could not overcome the forces trying to invade Riga, they made the following inscription on the façade:
Martin Luther. That is, if the story involves faith and it involves fighting with the church, then it goes through Riga.
The tour guides say that during the reconstruction were found several underpasses that allowed connecting the Blackheads house to the surrounding houses, the church and the port of the ship. And they were only found because in the reconstruction there were excavations to replace the foundations of the house, which was destroyed in 1941 by bombing during World War II.
Unfortunately he was one of the knights who did not leave his home on behalf of the Pope or the King. As Riga chief he chose to stay there and was eventually arrested, charged, and eventually burned to death in the central square.
For the harm they did to me.
Interestingly, they say the French King died a month later!
All this, within the 1 year deadline.
