Today we'll talk about Belgium, a country that is all about comics, beer and chocolates. I hope the reading is a delight!
In Antwerp, in addition to the train station, the local architecture is also impressive. The facades of the buildings, the old, the new, the modern, it is difficult to decide which style is better.
if you look closely, you will see some statues as if people were climbing a building. And suddenly you'll see one of them watching you.
After this visit you can stop at the Tolerance pub. And there the food is well served and delicious.
Ghent - the university city
One of the best cities in Belgium that inspired several comics such as: the Smurfs, The Adventures of Tim Tim among others. By the way, at the Atomium there is an exhibition made with the 30 human rights using only the comics, mostly Belgian, but there are others as well.
The Atomium is like the Eiffel Tower in Paris, only in Belgium. A steel structure made for an exhibition, but which was so well executed that the structure itself became the exhibition.
This pub entered the record books for offering more than 2.000 types of beers made by them. The menu looks more like an almanac of so many options.
Callebaut is the main Belgian chocolate shop, there are many different types and it is about 70 km from Brussels. Unfortunately, they didn't let us take pictures of the fabric like that, only those of the façade and reception are left.
Another legend has it that he tasted all the beers at the Delirium pub, and he's still peeing today. There's also the female version of it.
