Where you can see some things from Estonia. They even say that it is “a common thing for an Estonian” Like a rally, or climbing a mountain on a horse.
And finally, in addition to all this there is also a poster inviting you to be an Estonian citizen. And if you know English they promise to make the process as easy as possible.
Well, now let's get to what really matters. And how is public transport in Tallinn?
But that was when a young man approached us and started to say that transportation was free, that he himself, before obtaining his citizen card, had used public transportation for free and everything was fine. That if we wanted to save some change we could use it for free.
He turned to me as if he didn't know what I was talking about. Then I pointed to a poster written in Estonian that had a value.
And then I started to think… At the airport, they welcome us so well that we seem to be at home. The boy said that it was not necessary to pay for the ticket ...
And in fact it was true what the boy said!
In addition to the first reason already mentioned, which was for social inclusion and to allow all citizens to travel free of charge in Tallinn, there were also other effects caused by this measure.
Who knows, maybe you’re excited to put Estonia on your script?
