Well then it's time to keep the promise come on.
The second thing you will need is to know how to use the Paris subway. It is one of the oldest in Europe, yet it is very good and quite useful to move between the sights of the city.
One relevant observation is that it is divided into concentric zones. This means that if you imagine the zones in circles you will have Zone 1 in the smaller circle, Zone 2, with the same center of 1 in a larger circle, zone 3 in another bigger still, Zone 4 and finally zone 5 which is the farthest from the center.
so we have 5 zones and 16 subway lines that pass through these Zones. In fact the lines are from 1 to 14, having added to 3 bis and to 7 bis.
We have since a ticket, “single ride” that is valid until 1h: 30 min after the first validation, with all possible integrations within the same zone. combo of 10 tickets (single ride), with discount, up to ticket to "visit Paris" valid for 5 days, also passing by the option of valid for 24 hours.
Obviously each option has its price.
If you are staying in the center of Paris buy a combo of 10 tickets for the 1 zone. With them you can visit most of the sights and come back home without having to worry about this great variety of tickets.
On the first trip to Paris this was kind of hard to understand the first time, but we end up getting the hang of it, and with a couple of times or three times you'll be a part of it. Also because in the subway stations there is signalization of the direction of the subway.
To prevent someone else from using your 24 ticket for hours.
Well, now you want to know the best way to really visit Paris?
That's right, the city is so beautiful and has so much that you can move on foot on the way. and get back on the subway when you are most tired.
If on the way you managed to see your next tourist spot, go on foot. If you make a beautiful little one, go on foot.
When fate is far away and you are tired.
When it's cold to cut the ears.
When you want to go back to the apartment to rest.
I think the minimum required is from 4 to 5 days, after all the city has a lot to offer.
Yes, it is, but then you need to take a little more breath. And it can be a lot of rush.
