So today I'm going to talk a little bit about Uruguay. A country that is very different from South America, and why?
These changes have made Uruguay the most advanced country in South America with respect to fundamental rights, labor and free trade.
It did seem to innovate a lot in terms of legislation.
And all these measures were negotiated with the Uruguayan Chamber, having been proposed by Mujica, approved by the Chamber (Legislative Palace) and sanctioned by Mujica. Which shows his great negotiating power.
And to prove that it wasn't just small talk. Mujica donated about 90% of his salary as president to people in need.
“If we mix the desire to have money with politics, we are fried. Anyone who likes money a lot has to be taken out of politics.
