Other options are the shuttles offered by some more luxurious hotels, or even bus companies that provide such services.
And when you're traveling more economically, time and money are scarce. And then how to solve?
(Game Reserve) Am I not going to meet the Big 5?
It is a smaller nature reserve, much smaller compared to Kruger Park, with only 550 km². Which favors you on the one hand.
Pilanesberg is ideal for those who have little time in Johannesburg, would like to see the Big 5 and go on safari in 1 day.
In fact Pilanesberg Park is a complete park that allows you to live a unique experience and that you should think about if you are going to make a more economical and running trip.
But after all who are the "Big five" Or what is the Big 5 game?
Elephants live in herds and for me they should be considered the true kings of the jungle!
And they keep banging their heads until one of them gives up or dies in the process. So we learned that being tough-headed may not be a good idea.
As we could see in the video, even kings have their moments of laziness and leisure. In fact, lions have nocturnal habits and spend the day in a drowsiness like that!
This is the lion during the day!
Weighing between 40 to 90 kg and measuring just 0,90 cm under the 4 legs or 1,60 cm if seated he is the smallest animal on this list. This one knows how to hide, I didn't find any during the Reserve Game.
Perhaps they are relatives, I am not sure. And that's probably the leopard's best lesson, if you don't want to be found by someone who knows how to hide.
Well, now you already know who the big 5 are. On another occasion I talk about other animals, like hippos, zebras and giraffes!
What do the Mayans and Aztecs teach us about the pandemic?
If we look at a little more history we could learn and not repeat some mistakes.
Well, if you answer this question saying that it is because the Europeans were more developed than the American tribes, represented in particular by the Mayans and Aztecs (And the Incas too, but let's leave them for another post ok?!).
The acoustics of the Kukulcán pyramid and the Olympic Games arena in Chichén Itzá should also be highlighted. An applause at the base of the pyramid turns the sound of applause to a bird's song!
1- Represent one of the sacred animals of the Maya (A snake). I said it was also a temple of worship.
But why did the Mayans and Aztecs lose the fight to the Spanish?
1- Justinian's plague (Byzantine empire) that decimated 25 million people on 3 continents and lasted for some 200 years until humans were immune. (The famous herd immunity took 200 years to fight the first pandemic).
You know that story about washing your hands, wearing your mask, keeping a distance?
Thus, through sweat, contact, or the simple handshake to seal an agreement between Europeans and natives, it ended up causing a pandemic among the Mayans and Aztecs. 3- Fanaticism
And because they also believed in reincarnation, which is why the emperors were buried with some of their belongings and servants, the Mayans and Aztecs had a certain adoration for Europeans. Because in their calendar it marked that they were changing cycles, and they saw the Europeans coming from the waters, wearing very different clothes.
Summary: So my noble readers, that was how the civilizations: Maia, Aztec, and Inca were decimated by the Europeans.
And I hope that from now on you will make two reflections:
2- And the other reflection is that you should think about which religious leader are you following?
Does he say he is “sent by God” a Messiah?
And lead an entire people to destruction?
