These issues have been taken into account in investments. The proposal is to increase the incentives in ESG and thus guarantee a better quality in the execution of services, bringing environmental protection, social concern, including the increase in jobs and also the increase in added value for the company that chooses this model.
1- Employees, 2 shareholders, 3 customers, 4 suppliers, 5 Government agencies, 6 banks and financiers.
What is the company's gain with the use of ESG principles?
Increase in the Governance of the Company, which brings greater transparency and probably greater interest from investors to the companies. This also implies an appreciation of the company's shares.
There are several areas where it is considered possible to be a greenhouse gas reducer or polluter. What makes road, rail, air and port concessionaires, among others, fit into the ESG standard, and can qualify for the green bond market, the so-called Green Bounds.
There are already companies in Brazil that participate in this carbon market and are willing to negotiate, carry out consultancy for other interested companies and facilitate this accreditation. As an example, I mention ENGIE (Generator and transmitter of electric energy).
A little more about the use of ecological parks as a way of valuing the company
Depending on the project, these ecological park areas can also serve as carbon sink areas making carbon credits positive without major difficulties, reducing the environmental impact, protecting biodiversity and enabling the employment of the local community in these parks and thus reaffirming the social part of the ESG. This also brings appreciation to the group of investors who are concerned with this issue.
Well, first of all it is necessary to clarify that the ESG principles are optional and not mandatory. But if the company chooses to continue its business in the traditional way, that is, aiming only at profit, without concern for governance, the environment and society, which are the tripod of ESG, the company runs the risk of being left behind in this worldwide movement and see their stocks and shares melt on the stock exchange.
In the United States, it is already possible to compare the Sustainable Dow Jones Index with the average Dow Jones Index. In the graph below, we see a greater growth of companies that have adopted ESG standards.
Insurance companies or financial institutions that are guarantors of large projects are in the transition mode for issuing green bonds, the so-called “green bonds”.
Some countries, like the Netherlands, already have their own plan, in fact the Netherlands is a good example to be followed, their concern with climate change is due to the fact that it is a country below sea level, so the higher the global temperature, the greater the floods and the greater the possible damage. There may be a catastrophe with the breaking of dikes and dams.
India sought support from the Green Bound Principles and remains in line with sustainable international practices.
