How is it to fly with Qatar Airways?
She was so confused with me that she even took my passport and I still heard her playing a radio saying: "Yes, it's the orange suitcase".
When I passed customs, I was searched “chosen at random”. The bad thing is not going through the comb, the bad thing is having to reassemble your handbag that was made like an origami again.
In my case the passport. From a snack, chocolate or even a flag, you have to present the document!
I also saw a giant yellow teddy bear, which I nicknamed the Giant Picachu. I'm not sure what it means, but it serves as a meeting point.
The city of Doha is a destination where everything seems to be very luxurious and well maintained. It could not be otherwise since we are in the capital of Qatar.
In fact Qatar, as the first Islamic country I visited, I thought they were kind to the tourist and respectful too. They know that you are not Islamic and that is not why they are bothering you with this story.
And on the way back we discovered the rest area.
Remember to put your cell phone on silent when entering them. And the flight back had this peculiarity of allowing me to see the sun rise twice in the same day!
