What is a Land Trust?
We’ll explore that in-depth throughout this article.
There are many different types of land trusts, but Legal Dictionary defines the three most popular. The first type of land trust is a conservation land trust.
For the purposes of the rest of this article, we will focus on real estate land trusts and their benefits.
But wait – what about the Illinois land trust?
To find out more about creating a trust for property, let’s look at some of the pros and cons. How Stuff Works gives an in-depth look at this.
Another large benefit of a land trust is the ease of transferring ownership of the property to beneficiaries or heirs. Without a trust, an individual’s will has to be assessed through a costly legal process called probate, which involves paying back taxes and debt.
In simple terms, people use land trust for real estate ownership anonymity. On the other hand, people use living trusts to handle estate planning for personal assets.
