It may be that learning does not happen by making neuron connections, but rather by weeding out those that are not used.
In the first weeks of life, most babies will babble every possible sound imaginable.
Therefore, the child’s environment will play a tremendous role in brain development.
Imagine what your life could be like if you were able to stimulate your mind into activating even a small portion of that unused potential!
If I could have anything at all, what would it be?
What would I need to do to attain it?
What stops me from doing those things now?
How can I overcome those challenges to attain the life I desire?
