Performance is not an issue.
It’s one of the most powerful Android smartphones currently available.
Most smartphones heat up considerably when downloading a lot of data, such as when setting up a phone, but the Pixel didn’t.
It’s not yet available, so how it performs is still
It’s not the fastest charging smartphone available, but it’s considerably faster than Apple’s iPhone 7.
With an all-metal body, all-glass display, rock-solid build, fingerprint scanner and headphones socket, the Pixel ticks most of the boxes expected of top-end smartphone, except for a lack of waterproofing.
The Pixel is also the first smartphone to be certified for use with Google’s new DayDream virtual reality platform.
The USB and single speaker at the bottom (the left-side hole).
Using the Pixel as my primary device, it lasted just over 24 hours without charging, managing three hours of app usage and browsing, hundreds of emails and push notifications, a couple of photos, five hours of music over Bluetooth headphones and the odd game of Dan the Man during my one hour and 20-minute train commute to and from work.
The Pixel comes with the latest version of Android 7.1 Nougat and is the first smartphone to do so.
The biggest functional change for the home screen, however, is the new launcher shortcuts, which mirror Apple’s 3D touch gestures on iOS, but without the need for a pressure-sensitive screen.
A collection of Google Earth shots pan across a view of fields in Kent or the Pantheon in Rome, while live data wallpapers display battery charge levels, the current weather conditions, or the time.
Android 7.1 also now has a built-in night mode, which aims to reduce blue tones from the display to limit the amount of blue light shone into the eyes during the hours of darkness.
You can also only directly interact with Assistant via voice from the launcher, but you can type text into the Google search bar or in Allo.
To get the most out of it you must give your digital life over to Google and that certainly has some privacy implications – it knows where you are, what you’re searching for, can read what’s on the screen and collates all that data – but that isn’t a new phenomenon and is simply a progression of what Google’s been doing for the last couple of years on Android.
For UK users the Pixel phone and Google’s Allo app are the only two places Assistant is available for active interaction, but US users will also be able to buy Google Home, an Amazon Echo competitor.
Google Assistant isn’t a massive step forward in the AI wars, but it’s a solid start for Google in the next phase of conversational assistants.
Last year’s Google Nexus phones had brilliant fingerprint scanners on the back.
The Pixel’s 12.3-megapixel camera is cracking.
In good light you get crisp, well judged photos with an excellent amount of fine detail.
Low and poor light performance is also excellent, despite the camera not having optical image stabilisation, while the Google Camera app now has some much needed extra features, including the ability to switch the automatic white balance with the tap of a button and a golden ratio grid, which helps you frame your photos.
It only has one down-firing speaker on the bottom, which is easily blocked by hands when gaming
The notification LED is not enabled by default, but is available in notification settings
The calendar app now shows the correct date on the home screen
The design isn’t as innovative or interesting as that produced by Samsung.
Cons: not waterproof, no expandable memory, no front-facing speakers, no wireless charging, expensive
