7 Common Signs that You Still Have Mice or Rats In Your Home
Are those droppings you found under the cabinets old or new?
Following are some signs and tips for determining whether you have a current or previous rodent infestation in your home:
In contrast to the droppings, newer gnaw marks will be lighter in color and become darker as they age. These will often be found on food packaging or the structure of the house itself.
If an infestation is large, you may also detect an ongoing stale smell coming from hidden areas, indicating an active infestation.
Rodents will use materials such as shredded paper, fabric, or dried plant matter to make their nests. If these areas are found and have any of the other signs of current presence – fresh droppings, gnawing, odor or tracks – it is likely that there is still an infestation in your home.
If rodents are seen at night but never during the day, the population has probably not gotten too large and can be controlled with traps and bait. If you are seeing any rodents during the day, numerous fresh droppings or new gnaw marks, it is likely that the population has gotten quite large and may require professional services.
